1. DEFINITIONS
   1.1 "Software" means the HHMS hospital management system in any form —
       source code, object code, executables (including HHMS-Server.exe and
       HHMS-Client.exe), installers, updates, patches, documentation, UI
       designs, icons, database schemas, and derivative or modified works.
   1.2 "Personal Use" means non-commercial use by a single natural person on
       devices they own or control, for personal learning, evaluation, or
       home-record keeping, with no fee, revenue, patient-billing, or
       organizational deployment of any kind.
   1.3 "Non-Profit Organization" means a trust, society (Societies Registration
       Act, 1860 or the Gujarat Public Trusts Act, 1950), Section 8 company
       (Companies Act, 2013), NGO, charitable hospital, or government/aided
       medical institution whose profits, if any, are applied solely towards
       promoting its objects and are not distributed to its members.
   1.4 "Commercial User" means any person or entity that uses the Software for
       or in connection with any business, trade, profession, private
       hospital/clinic, for-profit educational activity, consultancy, service
       bureau, hosting, resale, or any activity generating revenue or monetary
       consideration, directly or indirectly.
   1.5 "Large Educational Institution" means any university, deemed university,
       medical/dental/homeopathic college, polytechnic, school of management or
       IT, or training institute (whether government or private, Aided or
       Un-Aided) that (a) has more than 500 enrolled students/staff, or
       (b) deploys the Software across more than 10 machines or multiple
       campuses, or (c) uses the Software in any paid program, workshop, lab,
       or for revenue-generating activity.
   1.6 "Written Permission" means a signed letter or email from the Licensor
       (or the Licensor's authorized representative) granting specific usage
       rights, obtained in advance, at licenses@hhms[dot]project[dot]example
       (replace with the Licensor's current published contact). An application,
       silence, or lapse of time never constitutes permission.
   1.7 "License Fees" means the fees quoted in a valid commercial proposal /
       purchase order accepted in writing by the Licensor, exclusive of GST at
       the prevailing rate.


